From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: openEuler RISC-V Maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tests: allow RISC-V emulation time for TLS reconnect

The blocking-timeout test deliberately blocks Redis for one second, so a
500 ms command timeout still proves that the command times out.  The upstream
10 ms margin is too short for the subsequent TLS reconnect handshake under
RISC-V linux-user emulation, where the same socket timeout is restored by
redisReconnect().  Increase only the RISC-V test margin; keep the timeout,
reconnect, TLS handshake, PING, and owned-parameter assertions enabled.

Upstream-Status: Not Submitted (automated upstream writes are forbidden)
Patch-Source: openEuler RISC-V QEMU CI run 31463568107
Patch-License: BSD-3-Clause
---
 test.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/test.c b/test.c
index 68d5ea1..02b09d8 100644
--- a/test.c
+++ b/test.c
@@ -1353 +1353,5 @@ static void test_blocking_connection_timeouts(struct config config) {
-    struct timeval tv = {.tv_sec = 0, .tv_usec = 10000};
+#if defined(__riscv)
+    struct timeval tv = {.tv_sec = 0, .tv_usec = 500000};
+#else
+    struct timeval tv = {.tv_sec = 0, .tv_usec = 10000};
+#endif
